# Dev Notes 60 — Runtime Event Log Store Runtime Wiring v1

**Date:** 2026-06-21  
**Branch:** `runtime-event-log-store-runtime-wiring-v1`  
**Status:** Candidate staged in assistant sandbox. Syntax checks, fixture coverage, worker import hygiene, targeted event-log integration smoke, existing event-log contract smoke, related action-event regression smokes, execute-action public dispatch smoke, nativeWorkerBackend execution mock smoke, action cancellation mock smoke, capability execute-action outcome smoke, and runtime public-entrypoint guard passed. Real-runtime testing has not been run in this assistant sandbox.

---

## 1. Purpose

This branch adds the smallest runtime-side integration seam between retained action-event publication and the existing event-log store contract.

The branch keeps the event-log store modular and non-durable by default:

```text
record action event into bounded in-memory history
  -> optional no-adapter event-log append handoff
  -> publish normalized event to live subscribers
```

The default runtime composition creates the event-log integration with no adapter, so current runtime behavior remains non-durable and no-op for event-log storage.

---

## 2. Scope

Implemented:

```text
runtime/bus/actionEventLog/actionEventLogIntegration.mjs
  createActionEventLogIntegration(...)
  appendRuntimeActionEventLog(...)

runtime.mjs
  creates a no-adapter event-log integration
  calls appendRuntimeActionEventLog(...) after in-memory history records the event

tests/smokeTestActionEventLogIntegration.mjs
  verifies no-adapter no-op behavior
  verifies sync and async adapter append observation
  verifies append failures are non-fatal
  verifies stream deltas remain high-volume excluded by default
  verifies source-boundary guards
```

Updated existing contract smoke source guard to allow the new modular integration seam while still forbidding runtime-owned adapter validation, concrete event-log backend naming, workerBridge coupling, and llama_worker coupling.

---

## 3. Explicit non-goals

Not implemented:

```text
no database adapter
no file adapter
no PostgreSQL/SQLite target
no eventLogStoreBackend implementation
no public runtime setter or config surface for adapters
no durable read API
no process-restart recovery
no cross-process pub/sub
no stream-delta retention or replay
no replacement of bounded in-memory history
no broad event manager
no workerBridge or llama_worker changes
```

The new integration helper is an optional append handoff only. It is not a storage backend and not a memory module.

